SUMMARY:Family Friendly Night Hike
DESCRIPTION:Bridge along Old Creedmoor trail. Photo by Don Kinney \nExplore the wonders of Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve at night!\nAs dusk falls\, we’ll set out along the Lizard's Loop Trail to investigate the sights and sounds of the forest after sunset.  Participants will discover fun facts about our local nocturnal critters and explore how your senses adjust to navigating in the dark. Remember to bring your flashlights or headlamps\, and a full bottle of water! This is a free\, family-friendly event\, but preregistration is required.
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/family-friendly-night-hike-3
LOCATION:Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve\, 13509 Old Creedmoor Rd\, Wake Forest\, NC\, 27587\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
